// A HALF CONSTRUCTOR OVER A FLOAT-TYPED PRODUCER.  cross() returns a
// float3 in the IR even on half inputs, so `half4(cross(...), p.w)` writes
// xyz as FLOAT data through the constructor's shared base register and only
// the w lane is half-typed.  A rule that stamps the whole register fp16 on
// the strength of that one lane reinterprets the xyz lanes - the value is
// wrong, not merely differently formatted (codex, review of t_cde25bad).
half4 main(half4 p : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR
{
	return half4(cross(p.xyz, p.zyx), p.w);
}
